# .gitignore for a Career Kit workspace ($CAREER_HOME).
#
# Copied here by `career-setup`. The workspace is private and it is its own git
# repo, which is the right default: you want history on your knowledge base, and
# a mistake in a rendered CV should be revertable.
#
# The problem is that "private repo" is a decision you make once and a `git push`
# is a decision you make at 1am. One day this workspace gets pushed somewhere,
# and on that day the ignore list below is the only thing standing between a
# public URL and other people's contact details.
#
# So the default is: an accidental push publishes a skeleton. Your knowledge
# base, your profile, your rules, your voice and your CV are all tracked, because
# those are yours and losing them hurts. Everything that contains someone ELSE's
# data, or that is rebuildable, is ignored.
#
# Un-ignore something only when you have decided it is safe, one line at a time.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party personal data. This is the part that must never be public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# One JSON file per target. Holds company contacts, recruiter names, and
# whatever a posting or a reply contained. Real job records have carried a
# founder's personal mobile number and a private home address.
jobs/

# Per-target drafts: the email bodies you wrote, including anything you decided
# not to send, plus form answers and cover letters naming individual people.
drafts/

# Proof that a form submit happened: screenshots of a submitted application,
# confirmation pages, PDFs. Screenshots of a filled form show every field you
# typed, which is your address and phone number rendered as an image.
outputs/receipts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived state. Rebuildable, and it leaks the shape of your search.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The board, rebuilt from jobs/ by `career-board`. It is every company on one
# page with what you did about each, which is the same disclosure as career.db
# below and easier to open by accident, because it is a web page.
outputs/board.html

# The tracker DB, rebuilt from jobs/ by `career-review`. Publishing it publishes
# every company you applied to, when, with what outcome, and your salary notes.
# The -wal and -shm files hold recent writes that have not landed in the DB yet,
# so ignoring only career.db leaks the last few transactions.
career.db
career.db-wal
career.db-shm

# Append-only gate history: every claim, send, block and resolve, with
# timestamps. A complete log of who you contacted and when.
.ledger.jsonl

# In-flight leases. Short-lived, machine-local, and they name the target of an
# action that has not finished yet. Committing one also breaks the lock: a lease
# arriving by `git pull` blocks a claim on a machine where nothing is running.
.leases/

# The previewer's per-boot auth token. It is the only credential guarding a
# local server that writes files. Never commit a credential, even a local one,
# even one that rotates.
.previewer-token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracked on purpose, listed here so the decision is visible:
#   profile.yaml        your identity. Yours, and the file forms read from.
#   rules.yaml          your doctrine. Worth history.
#   voice.md            expensive to re-derive. Worth history most of all.
#   knowledge-base.md   the source of truth.
#   cv/                 including the canonical PDF.
#   outputs/brief.md    generated, but small and useful to diff.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
